1062 #uuid "59bc86e8-4dae-564b-ab2b-c8ac5309d3be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134756 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186135083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134757 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134757 #edb/ref 1061 25909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134757 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9095d8fd-3ce2-5af6-bda4-4a49a820addf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134757 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134758 #edb/ref 1061 25911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134758 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bb2a0a7b-340c-53a3-a510-9a559cc6d898" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134758 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135082 #edb/ref 1064 "How do we represent the double integral of a function over a non-rectangular region as a repeated integral? \n\nSpecifically, let's consider\n![](images/3a/3ac99dd8336c3a877fbf6ba63a3074a490b85c8a350adad00da423412dd60ee3.svg)\n\nwhere ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg)  is the finite region enclosed by the lines ![](images/df/df9822243c11ec9f0fabca5cc578976d0bdea2c521b4f61964f5f3850a970504.svg), ![](images/1f/1fb9f2f73a09599931892c1dee7629975b4d851e5dd6f0d07b7c641bbf17bf54.svg), ![](images/23/238e977be23f692486c8bf68f6b40255435b3d1796cc50d260a014a8c670be7b.svg) and ![](images/b5/b5489c125683eb29c2cababe2e1b7094d6a16b89d09970c42af649df70d045e4.svg) as shown below.\n\n![](images/af/af0a1a74df8aec0d5189dc2402fc1840c25d4cd94d8861fa06110cae7b449843.png)\n\nFirst, notice that ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) is a *type I* region. \nTo determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](images/39/39629b33e25aed05bf9a5ca36180f984e7ff8f863c6966d47f60483d672a8af4.png)\n\nSo, the region ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) can be defined as \n\n![](images/78/78cf2ea7f960497f7cc9beea602bf6ca0e82b74491f9f56cce76130d965d4a64.svg)\n\nNow, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n![](images/3c/3c423b0d423203621ab89258a6fff4cea190279b4dcc7170c8a7070bf1f85e24.svg)\n\nAnd that's our answer! Notice that, when we have a type I region, \n\n- the limits for ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) are functions of ![](images/5a/5aac2c81021f3f9e468e7840c5f95ece35c10b894bdae19ec1d247bdeb47ac6f.svg)\n\n- the limits for ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) are constants, and\n\n- we integrate over the variable ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) before integrating over the variable ![](images/cf/cff7b257e3c71ec70dc7cd273bdd1cced4254993a43cffbfc338460c21bc7319.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135082 #edb/ref 1065 4261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135082 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7c641021-bc5e-5b05-8a23-b198735ee5a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135082 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135083 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we want to evaluate the repeated integral\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{x}^{2x} (x-2y) \\ \\mathrm{d}  y \\ \\mathrm{d}  x.\n$$\n\nNotice that the domain of integration is a type I region. \n\nTo compute this integral, we must bear the following important points in mind.\n\n- We start with the inner integral, as usual.\n\n- When integrating with respect to $y,$ we treat $x$ as though it were a constant.\n\n- The limits of integration for the inner integral are functions of $x.$ Once again, we treat $x$ as though it were a constant and substitute the integration limits as usual. After this step, there should be no more $y$'s in our integral.\n\n- Finally, we compute the outer integral.\n\nLet's apply these steps to solve the given problem.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{x}^{2x}(x-2y)\\text{ }dy]\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[xy-{y}^{2}]_{x}^{2x}\\text{ }dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[x\\cdot (2x)-{(2x)}^{2}]-[x\\cdot (x)-(x)^{2}]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[2{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}]-[{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-2{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,dx & =-2{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{[{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}[{1}^{3}-{0}^{3}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135083 #edb/ref 1065 4262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135083 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3698e7e3-4bc2-5db0-96b5-172131284b4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135083 #edb/ref 1067 "Evaluating Repeated Integrals With Variable Limits" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267638 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267638 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267638 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a55a9b55-701b-54b8-9dc3-ff767eb9a16b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267800 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267800 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267800 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b89fe4b4-ca5f-5b19-9c79-5f2ac46d2595" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267859 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267859 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267859 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bf6a5ad1-907d-59c7-a9c8-ed050fde1508" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268207 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268207 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268207 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e85875be-4289-5cdd-8c4f-d83917f81081" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268375 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268375 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268375 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fcfb32be-1877-5c91-86e5-ee84568b6b69" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268681 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268681 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268681 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268681 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186268207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268681 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186268375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268681 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268681 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268681 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186268375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268681 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9bb0802c-c72d-5b84-a668-8e4527960b23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268853 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268853 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132276" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268853 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268853 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dy\\,dx=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268853 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "07938b36-7b86-5365-9a53-980eadb141d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268853 #edb/ref 1074 "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x[\\,y\\,]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,dx & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-2) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321192 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{11}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321192 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321192 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04d2a009-9a40-5d25-99e2-4f97af963231" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321242 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321242 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321242 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b726bfa-ba4c-5d91-9f6d-6a3764d8755d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321322 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321322 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321322 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1594e17d-7011-5f7d-aa6a-12336ec25a8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321479 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321479 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321479 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2b5f94c5-0d1b-5f79-944c-8cb9d821beed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321490 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{6}{11}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321490 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321490 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2c533ee8-f9db-5f4a-a560-8035da471b44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321590 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{3}{11}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321590 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321590 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3a0552d2-cfa6-5c1e-901c-be3cad62fa64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321828 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321828 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045